{
  "schema_version": "1.9.2",
  "id": "USN-9125-1",
  "summary": "ssvnc vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that SSVNC incorrectly handled certain CoRRE rectangles,\nleading to a heap buffer overflow. A malicious VNC server could possibly\nuse this issue to cause SSVNC to crash, resulting in a denial of service,\nor possibly execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2018-20020)\n\nIt was discovered that SSVNC incorrectly handled certain raw rectangles,\nleading to an infinite loop. A malicious VNC server could possibly use this\nissue to cause SSVNC to consume excessive resources, leading to a denial of\nservice. (CVE-2018-20021)\n\nIt was discovered that SSVNC did not properly initialize certain messages\nsent to the server. A malicious VNC server could possibly use this issue to\nobtain sensitive information. (CVE-2018-20022)\n\nIt was discovered that SSVNC did not check for memory allocation failures\nin its zlib and ZRLE decoders, leading to a NULL pointer dereference. A\nmalicious VNC server could possibly use this issue to cause SSVNC to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2018-20024)",
